WhatsApp older chats on request (mautrix-whatsapp v0.2610.0).

The bridge stores every conversation the phone sends at pairing (history sync) but creates rooms only for the newest
max_initial_conversations of them, once. Unichat's "Load older chats" needs the rest: `!whatsapp sync-history-chats <n>`
(n from 1 to 500, the command's own login, no admin) runs createPortalsFromHistorySync with limit n, which takes the
n most recent conversations not synced since this login, and replies "Created <k> chats from history sync" (k: the
rooms queued). The function now takes its limit and returns that count; the startup call passes the config's, as before.
A bad n replies with usage. history_sync_portals_need_creating is left alone: it only schedules the startup run.
Applied by .github/workflows/natives.yml (git apply), for macOS and Windows.

